From c57da41302fb2e95fe65ffb6a03174b9c1a7240b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Moeijiro <Moeijiro@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 12:23:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Redesign for scanning; add StudyRaid

Homepage rebuilt around what a visitor needs in the first seconds: who,
what, the stack, featured projects and a contact link. The depth moves one
click away.

- Hero with name, role, one-line pitch, CTAs and computed proof points
- Five featured projects chosen for range, StudyRaid leading
- Cards answer what it is, why it is interesting and what it is built with
  (new plain-language pitch/why fields); screenshot on every card
- Projects page: uniform grid, animated category filters incl. AI
- Compact capability cards, primary stack chips, condensed quality list
- System diagram, principles and counted stack moved to About
- Case studies: plain lead, jump links, screenshots first, security and
  testing sections
- StudyRaid case study, screenshots, code excerpt and social image
- Scroll reveals no longer hide server-rendered content
- og.mjs: ONLY= subset and FONTS_DIR= offline rendering

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DwYkai8vQVSo59fBXVzGXq
